==French==

===Etymology===
{{lit|there is an [[eel]] [[hidden]] [[beneath]] a [[rock]]}}. Compare also {{cog|la|latet anguis in herbā}} (whence {{cog|en|snake in the grass}}), as well as {{cog|nl|addertje onder het gras}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA|y‿avoir‿anguille sous roche}}
* {{audio|fr|LL-Q150 (fra)-Lyokoï-y avoir anguille sous roche.wav}}

===Verb===
{{fr-verb}}

# {{lb|fr|impersonal|figuratively}} for there to be something [[fishy]] and [[suspicious]] going on, for there to be something [[in the wind]], [[in the offing]]
#: {{uxi|fr|il y a anguille sous roche|I [[smell a rat]]; something is [[afoot]].}}

